# SRG-APP-000860-AU-000350  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must for password-based authentication, allow user
# selection of long passwords and passphrases, including spaces and all
# printable characters.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000860-AU-000350
group:           V-263579
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004064
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk places no maximum length on a native password and excludes no
                 printable character from one, so long passphrases are permitted by the
                 product as shipped; what it can be configured to do is require length,
                 through authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength, which the
                 product STIG sets to 15 or more. One product limitation applies: the spec
                 states the semicolon is not allowed by the special-character rule, so that
                 one printable character is not available for the minPasswordSpecial count.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength min 15
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.2.2510/manage-credentials-and-keys/configure-a-splunk-enterprise-password-policy-using-the-authentication.conf-configuration-file
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, the permitted length and
                 character set are enforced by the directory service or identity provider,
                 not by Splunk.
external:        Entry of spaces and non-ASCII printable characters at the client - carried
                 by the browser and the workstation's keyboard handling.
external:        The organization's own minimum and maximum length policy -
                 organization-defined; the value asserted here is the one the product STIG
                 sets for this product.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:441 (minPasswordLength, default
                 8, no maximum), :477 (minPasswordSpecial - "The semicolon character is not
                 allowed"); SPLK-CL-000370 check and fix text
finding:         The application does not require long passwords for native accounts -
                 authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength is missing or 14 or
                 less, leaving the spec default of 8 or a weaker configured value in force;
                 this determination is from the perspective of the application layer alone,
                 and note that the product reserves the semicolon from the
                 special-character rule, which is a product limitation rather than a
                 configuration shortfall.
